      "verdict": "0 of 5 candidate rules reproduce ρ for all 4 atoms in the B_3 registry (['proton', 'neutron', 'deuteron', 'he3']).  H_3-level χ_λ collisions: [['proton', 'neutron', 'he3']] (all groups); falsifying subset (different ρ within group): [['proton', 'neutron', 'he3']].  Atoms in the falsifying subset are Markov-equivalent at the braid strand count yet have distinct ρ — no (chi, y)-only rule can distinguish them.  Same-ρ collisions (e.g. proton vs neutron) are benign.  The structural fix per conj:rho-prefactor-structural is to evaluate the rule at the *atomic* strand count n_0 = 3·A, embedding the braid into H_{3·A} via the binding operator K (Hopf for ²H, L6a4 for ³He, ...).  This requires Hoefsmit at H_6 / H_9 — deferred.",
